WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.472
Workflow, not agent.

2
00:00:01.752 --> 00:00:15.597
Anthropic’s “Building effective agents” post separates workflows, where code decides the sequence of steps and models fill in particular steps, from agents, where the model decides what to do next and which tools to use.

3
00:00:15.877 --> 00:00:22.171
It recommends starting with the simplest solution that works and adding autonomy only when the task needs it.

4
00:00:22.451 --> 00:00:23.987
This feature is a workflow.

5
00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:33.696
The steps are known in advance and always the same: read the transcript, find candidate items, check them, normalize them, merge duplicates, ask a human.

6
00:00:33.976 --> 00:00:40.248
Letting a model choose the order buys nothing and costs you predictability, testability, and cost control.

7
00:00:40.528 --> 00:00:49.829
You will still use tool calling from lessons 10 and 11, but inside a stage, with a bounded loop, for the specific job of resolving owners and dates.
